    [process_name] => lemon production – MX – lemon
    [category] => Agriculture, Forestry, Fishing and Hunting/111 Crop Production
    [general_comment] => This dataset represents the production of 1 kg of lemons. The average yield from 2009 - 2012 is 13.8 t/ha. The data are representative for lemons production in Mexico used for the export market. Mineral NPK fertiliser input is 33-0-10 kg/ha. Organic fertilisers applied amount to 1.67 m3/ha of liquid manure and 1.07 t/ha of solid manure. Total active ingredients (a.i.) applied as pesticides amount to 28.6 kg a.i./ha. The dataset was modelled within the project 'World Food LCA database (WFLDB)'. The aim of this project was to provide inventories of a broad variety of agricultural products and processes and to cover for each product at least 50% of the global export market. The export share of lemons produced in Mexico amounts to 18% of the global export (tonnage exported in 2010). The production system regarded in this dataset aimed at representing lemons produced in Mexico for the export market. PEF-Quality: data quality rating (DQR) = 3.2 (i.e. fair quality). This dataset refers to an average situation; for specific situations exchanges might differ substantially due to site specific parameters. The system boundary starts with the nursery producing fruit tree seedlings and ends with the waste treatment after the clearing of the orchard. It includes all activities of a year in the productive phase, the establishment phase, and the clearing of the orchard including waste treatment.
    [technology_description] => 
    [geo_description] => 
