    [process_name] => EPD: SANDWICH PANELS ISODECK PVSTEEL TPO-PVC WITH STEEL FACINGS AND INSULATING CORE OF POLYURETHAN OR POLYSOCINURATE FOAM
    [category] => Manufacturing/332 Fabricated Metal Product Manufacturing/332311 Prefabricated Metal Building and Component Manufacturing
    [general_comment] => Environmental Product Declaration for 1 m² of Isodeck PVSteel PU - PVC insulating roof panel with an insulation thickness of 80 mm and steel sheet thickness of 0.8 mm (external with membrane) + 0.5 mm (internal). The study follows a 'cradle-to-gate with options' approach, including modules A1-A5 (product stage, construction), C1-C4 (end-of-life), and D (benefits and loads beyond the system boundary). The panel consists of two external pre-painted galvanized steel supports enclosing an insulating core of polyurethane or polyisocyanurate foam. The results of this EPD are also applicable to the Isodeck PVSteel PU TPO (with the same insulation core thickness and sheet metal).
    [technology_description] => 
