e chemicals used in water conditioning. Sustain 11. Üçtuğ, F.G., 2019. The environmental life cycle assessment of dairy products. Food Eng. Rev. 11, 104–121. Vicencio-de la Rosa, M.G., Valencia-Vázquez, R., Pérez-López, M.E., Martínez-Prado, M. A., Ramírez-Ramírez, E.S., 2015. Stabilization by co-composting of solids removed from wastewater treatment plant of a cheese factory. Rev. Mex. Ing. química 14, 61–71.
    [modeling_constants] => The functional unit was 1 kg of Oaxaca cheese. The life cycle analysis was characterized from the reception of raw milk at the producer's door until the exit of the product for retail sale. Data on milk production was left out of the system, although the raw material (milk) was considered as an input. Whey was considered an avoided product because it is re-used as food by pig farms. It was considered that 10% of whey is lost and allocated to wastewater.
